This project uses **split graphify graphs** (not `graphify update .` on repo root). Full guide: [.cursor/docs/graphify.md](../docs/graphify.md).

## Graphs

| Graph | `--graph` path | Use when |
|-------|----------------|----------|
| JS port | `js/graphify-out/graph.json` | Wiring inside `js/` |
| C reference | `nethack-c/graphify-out/graph.json` | `nethack-c/upstream/{src,include}` semantics |
| Merged | `graphify-out/graph.json` | C↔JS `path`, cross-tree `query` / `explain` |

## After code changes

- Edited **`js/`** → `npm run graphify:js` (or `bash tools/graphify-update.sh js`)
- Submodule / **C reference** work → `npm run graphify:c`
- Need merged graph after either side changed → `npm run graphify:merge`

## Query discipline

When a graph exists, prefer `graphify query` / `path` / `explain` with the **smallest** graph above and `--graph <path>`. Read per-tree `GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad review — not the deprecated monolithic root scan.

**Never** `graphify update .` on the repo root (slow; indexes tools/sessions/docs).
